The full 02_align execution order:

Step 1 - align class1 and class2:
    bash scripts/02_align/run_mafft.sh \
        data/processed/class1_sequences.fasta \
        results/alignments/class1_aligned.fasta \
        --threads 8

    bash scripts/02_align/run_mafft.sh \
        data/processed/class2_sequences.fasta \
        results/alignments/class2_aligned.fasta \
        --threads 8

Step 2 - entropy (optionally with baselines):
    python scripts/02_align/entropy.py

    python scripts/02_align/entropy.py \
        --baseline-conserved data/external/conservation_baseline/rplA_aligned.fasta \
        --baseline-divergent data/external/conservation_baseline/mfs_transporter_aligned.fasta

A few design notes worth knowing:

run_mafft.sh takes an input FASTA and output path directly. It uses --auto mode -
MAFFT automatically picks L-INS-i for small datasets and FFT-NS-2 for large ones.
With many sequences, both classes will use FFT-NS-2.
The skip flag prevents re-running completed alignments. The same script is used
for baseline sequences - just pass the downloaded FASTA and a target path.

entropy.py computes Shannon entropy over all MSA columns, then filters scores
to only the columns where the E. coli reference sequence has a residue. This maps
scores back to reference positions (0-548 for Class I, 0-467 for Class II),
matching the x-axis in the figure. The known catalytic residues (Cys105/224/318
for Class I, His188/Ser318/Lys324/Glu331 for Class II) are mapped directly onto
the filtered scores using the E. coli UniProt ID (P0AC33/P05042) from config.py
QUERIES to locate the reference sequence, so the per-position CSV will flag them
as is_functional_site=True - ready for figure coloring downstream.

The --baseline-conserved/divergent flags are for entropy context comparison.
Baseline sequences can be fetched using scripts/02_align/download_baselines.py,
then aligned with run_mafft.sh before passing to entropy.py:

    python scripts/02_align/download_baselines.py

    bash scripts/02_align/run_mafft.sh \
        data/external/conservation_baseline/rplA.fasta \
        data/external/conservation_baseline/rplA_aligned.fasta \
        --threads 8

    bash scripts/02_align/run_mafft.sh \
        data/external/conservation_baseline/mfs_transporter.fasta \
        data/external/conservation_baseline/mfs_transporter_aligned.fasta \
        --threads 8

Or fetch manually from UniProt:
    RplA (conserved):
        https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/stream?query=gene:rplA+AND+reviewed:true&format=fasta
    MFS transporter (divergent):
        https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/stream?query=family:"major+facilitator+superfamily"+AND+reviewed:true&format=fasta&size=500
